RF.put("questb:b25",{"8665":{"id":8665,"t":"Genesis Boots","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of Rebirth, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Silver Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj. This quest also requires Neutral faction with the Brood of Nozdormu.\nQiraji Bindings of Dominance Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Rebirth Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"Qiraji magic is strong and ancient. The most powerful qiraji wield items of such might, they'd give pause even to a dragon.\nBring me the qiraji bindings of dominance and other minor components by and I'll create a set of powerful boots for you.\nYou will find them useful in the fight against the enemy.","rew":"You will receive:\nGenesis Boots\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹name›. You've proven you're no ordinary mortal.\nI give you these with the confidence they'll aid you in crushing the vile qiraji.\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Druid Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8665\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Genesis Boots this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Dominance, 2 Idols of Rebirth, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Silver Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8505":{"id":8505,"t":"The Alliance Needs Purple Lotus!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 37.","obj":"Bring 20 Purple Lotus to Master Nightsong at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n20 Purple Lotus Elder Torntusk 40 % , Constrictor Vine 1.9 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 1.9 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 1.9 % and 4 more","desc":"‹class›, the purple lotus is a flower with a plentitude of uses. I am here at the request of the Alliance as an authority on those applications, to preserve the herbs collected and to ensure that their war effort acquires enough purple lotus to sustain whatever function they plan for it.\nI would like for you to travel out into the world and return to me with some of these flowers. Is that something that you can do?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Do you have the purple lotus herbs that I requested?","done":"Your contribution is greatly appreciated, ‹class›. It is only through the combined efforts of all that we shall be able to repel the ruthless advance of the silithid and whatever force is driving them forth. Even the Horde is amassing their own collection of purple lotus. Should you come across more, please return to me here.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.6,"y":32.5,"n":"Master Nightsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"505":{"id":505,"t":"Syndicate Assassins","lv":33,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 12 Syndicate Footpads and 8 Syndicate Thieves, then return to Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore.\nSyndicate Footpad slain : 0/ 12\nSyndicate Thief slain : 0/ 8","desc":"I am the new magistrate of Southshore, recently assigned after the assassination of the previous magistrate. The assassins were never found, but through our investigations we're almost certain they were hired by the Syndicate - a group of thieves led by villainous nobles of the now fallen kingdom of Alterac.\nThe Syndicate has a camps in Sofera's Naze and Corahn's Dagger, north and west of the Horde-occupied Tarren Mill. Slay the Syndicate members you find in these camps.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCrusader Belt Insulated Sage Gloves\nExperience: 1,950\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You have slain those Syndicate thugs, I trust?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Although they may still be lurking about, we hope that some of the thieves and footpads you slew were responsible for the last magistrate's death. But even if they weren't, the Syndicate is a taint on this land and a stain on the human race.\nTheir deaths are welcome to Southshore.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":48.1,"y":59.1,"n":"Magistrate Henry Maleb","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"6985":{"id":6985,"t":"Irondeep Supplies","lv":55,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 55 instead of 60. Pays 85s instead of 0.","obj":"Bring 10 Irondeep Supplies to the Horde Quartermaster in Frostwolf Keep.\n10 Irondeep Supplies Irondeep Supplies in Alterac Valley","desc":"The Stormpike dwarves are using the Irondeep mine as a storage depot. I want you to raid that mine and bring me its supplies. This will curtail the Stormpikes' efforts in Alterac Valley, and will provide us with needed equipment!\nBe wary, ‹name›. The Irondeep mine is deep in Alliance territory, and control of the mine is as shifting as the snows of Alterac.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Did you enter the Irondeep mine, ‹name›? Did you raid its supplies?","done":"You got them! Nicely done, ‹name›! And I hope you saw a few dwarves during your raid, and shed their blood for the Frostwolves!\nStart Frostwolf Quartermaster Alterac Valley End Frostwolf Quartermaster Alterac Valley Level 55 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 53 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6985","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7385":{"id":7385,"t":"A Gallon of Blood","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"null\n5 Stormpike Soldier's Blood Winterax Mystic , Syndicate Agent , Syndicate Brigand , Alliance Sentinel and 4 more","desc":"You have the option of offering larger quantities of the blood taken from our enemies. I will be glad to accept gallon sized offerings, ‹name›.","back":"You have the option of offering larger quantities of the blood taken from our enemies. I will be glad to accept gallon sized offerings, ‹name›.","done":"The blood of our enemies has been shed. I shall mix this blood with the rest that has been gathered. Once the offering is complete, the Ice Lord shall show these Stormpike dogs the full wrath of the Frostwolf Clan!\nStart Primalist Thurloga Alterac Valley End Primalist Thurloga Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7385","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"6825":{"id":6825,"t":"Call of Air - Guse's Fleet","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Stormpike Soldier's Flesh Alliance Sentinel , Stormpike Mountaineer , Frostwolf in Alterac Valley , Winterax Troll and 4 more","back":"We must prepare the new fleet of War Riders, ‹race›! My riders are set to make a strike on the central battlefield; but first, I must wet their appetites - preparing them for the assault.\nI need enough Stormpike Soldier Flesh to feed a fleet! Hundreds of pounds! Surely you can handle that, yes? Get going!","done":"The fleet feeds on their flesh. It consumes the enemy.\nFlight is imminent!\nStart Wing Commander Guse Alterac Valley End Wing Commander Guse Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6825","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"8105":{"id":8105,"t":"The Battle for Arathi Basin!","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Assault the mine, the lumber mill, the blacksmith and the farm, then return to Field Marshal Oslight in Refuge Pointe.\nMine Assaulted\nLumber Mill Assaulted\nBlacksmith Assaulted\nFarm Assaulted","desc":"‹name›, the battle for Arathi Basin is a battle for resources and territory. Key points in the area must be held and operated in order to supply our forces with much needed raw materials and supplies. I charge you to assault the points farthest from our Arathi Basin base.\nAssault the farm, the mine, the lumber mill and the blacksmith when they are controlled by the enemy. Find the enemy's banner and rip it from its flag post!\nWhen you have done this to all four points, return to me.","rew":"Money: 1 65 1 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650\n+200 reputation with The League of Arathor","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":45.8,"y":45.5,"n":"Field Marshal Oslight","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"8265":{"id":8265,"t":"Defiler's Advanced Care Package","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nDefiler's Advanced Care Package\nExperience: 650\n+10 reputation with The Defilers","done":"You've certainly begun to prove yourself to us, ‹name›. As a reward, please take this care package! Inside it you'll find rations and bandages that are usable only inside Arathi Basin.\nAs you continue to prove yourself inside the Basin, you'll find that these items will become available to you for purchase. Rations become available when you are Honored with us, and bandages when you are Revered.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.4,"y":29.7,"n":"Rutherford Twing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"665":{"id":665,"t":"Sunken Treasure","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Professor Phizzlethorpe to the cave and back.","desc":"Now that we are full-fledged Blackwater Raiders it is our job to help Mr. O'Breen locate the lost elven treasure.\nIt is next to impossible to find the gems in the dark sea without aid. The doctor has constructed some goggles that will help. He needs the goggles charged with the energy derived from the enchanted stone in the cave just up the hill.\nBut the cave is cursed! When we get close, we get ambushed. Defend me and I can harness the energy from the stone into the goggles.","rew":"Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"This is no time to talk! The goggles need to be charged with the power of the stone!","done":"The goggles work perfectly now! Well done, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":33.9,"y":80.5,"n":"Professor Phizzlethorpe","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":33.9,"y":80.4,"n":"Doctor Draxlegauge","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"25":{"id":25,"t":"Stonetalon Standstill","lv":25,"min":23,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Dispatch 12 Befouled Water Elementals at Mystral Lake, due east of the Talondeep Path and southwest of Splintertree Post.\nScout the gazebo on Mystral Lake that overlooks the nearby Alliance outpost.\nReturn to Mastok Wrilehiss at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.\nBefouled Water Elemental slain : 0/ 12","desc":"If you want to be useful, then why don't you do something about the situation near Talondeep Path?\nThe transports between Ashenvale and Stonetalon are at a standstill because of the lake coming alive and attacking anything that gets close... which means anyone on the path. What'd be even more useful than just putting the hammer down on the water elementals there is someone scouting the gazebo on Mystral Lake - the one that has a solid view of the Alliance outpost there.\nYou up for being useful?","rew":"Money: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,000\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"You back already? What's the situation out there - all cleared up now, thanks to you?","done":"Yeah, I heard that someone tore up the lake out there like a dust devil through the Barrens. From the sound of it too, we might be able to set up a possible observation area out there to keep an eye on our Alliance friends. Well, that is if we can keep it on the down low...\nLooks like you ended up being quite useful after all; the transports between here and Stonetalon should have an easier time of it. Take this - you've earned it.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":73.7,"y":60,"n":"Mastok Wrilehiss","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"7865":{"id":7865,"t":"Sentinel Advanced Care Package","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nSentinel Advanced Care Package\nExperience: 650\n+10 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","done":"You've certainly begun to prove yourself to us, ‹name›. As a reward, please take this care package! Inside it you'll find rations and bandages that are usable only inside Warsong Gulch.\nAs you continue to prove yourself inside the Gulch, you'll find that these items will become available to you for purchase. Rations become available when you are Friendly with us, and bandages when you are Honored.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":61.5,"y":83.9,"n":"Illiyana Moonblaze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"8985":{"id":8985,"t":"More Components of Importance","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire a Starbreeze Village Relic and return it to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.\nStarbreeze Village Relic Frostmaul Preserver , Frostmaul Giant","desc":"‹class›, listen closely. Now that we have the location of the last amulet piece, we still need another component to suffuse the brazier with; something that will provide a focus strong enough to entice the spirit of my deceased, former comrade.\nIsalien, our priestess, grew up in Winterspring at Starbreeze Village. I need you to gather a Starbreeze Village Relic from the Frostmaul giants of Frostwhisper Gorge in southern Winterspring, who are known for raiding to the north from time to time.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n3 Bloodkelp Elixir of Dodging 3 Bloodkelp Elixir of Resistance\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you returned already then, ‹class›, with what I sent you out to gather?","done":"A job well done, ‹name›. I will imbue the essence of the relic into the brazier.\nNow all that is left is to go to the Shrine of Eldretharr in the east wing of Dire Maul, and use the brazier to summon forth the spirit of my former cohort, Isalien. Her spirit has been corrupted by her possession of the piece of Valthalak's amulet, and the portion of his soul within it.\nOh, by the way, I had some leftover bloodkelp from your trip to Alcaz Isle, so I made it into some potions for you. Take your pick!\nBurning Steppes Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"5305":{"id":5305,"t":"Sweet Serenity","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Stratholme and kill the Crimson Hammersmith. Recover the Crimson Hammersmith's Apron and return to Lilith.\nCrimson Hammersmith's Apron Crimson Hammersmith","desc":"Within the confines of the Scarlet Bastion lies sweet Serenity. The Crimson Hammersmith guards the recipe with his life. Defeat him and bring me his apron. For that, I shall reward you with the knowledge required to create an enchanted battlehammer!","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Enchanted Battlehammer\nExperience: 8,300","back":"His apron! Where is it?","done":"May you bash in many a brain, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.3,"y":37.1,"n":"Lilith the Lithe","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"2585":{"id":2585,"t":"The Decisive Striker","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring three Scorpok Pincers, two Vulture Gizzards, and one Blasted Boar Lung to Bloodmage Drazial.\n3 Scorpok Pincer Scorpok Stinger 40 % , Clack the Reaver 30 %\n2 Vulture Gizzard Black Slayer 40 % , Spiteflayer 30 %\nBlasted Boar Lung Ashmane Boar 40 % , Helboar 40 % , Grunter 30 %","desc":"Have you ever watched them in battle, ‹name›? The scorpoks, I mean. Have you ever seen the grace and agility with which they move? The decisiveness of their strikes?\nIf only we could somehow isolate that agility and encapsulate it, we would be wealthy beyond our... I mean... it would be a boon for the scientific community.\nAssist me, ‹name›, and I shall allow you a sampling of the assay.\nIn order to create a stable sample, I will need three scorpok pincers, two vulture gizzards, and one blasted boar lung.","rew":"You will receive:\nGround Scorpok Assay\nExperience: 4,700","back":"Where are the organs, ‹name›!?","done":"Fascinating. This has been the most difficult of all assays to analyze.\nTake a pinch of this residual salt and place it under your tongue. You should experience a slight feeling of euphoria followed by a state of unprecedented agility and quickness.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":50.6,"y":14.2,"n":"Bloodmage Drazial","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"4185":{"id":4185,"t":"The True Masters","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Highlord Bolvar Fordragon after speaking with Lady Katrana Prestor.","desc":"Solomon paints a dreary picture. Still, we cannot afford to send our thinly spread troops to the aid of Lakeshire on speculation. I will need proof of these claims before I can act.\nSpeak with Lady Prestor, ‹name›. She is a learned woman and knows much of dragons and dragonkin. She may be able to shed some light on this situation.","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"<Bolvar watches you intently.>","done":"<Bolvar cups his chin as if in deep thought.>\nWhile I respect Lady Prestor's stance, I believe that there is a solution to this dilemma that may put all of our concerns to rest.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"94265":{"id":94265,"t":"Craftsmans writ goblin rocket fuel","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Goblin Rocket Fuel\nGoblin Rocket Fuel","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Goblin Rocket Fuel, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Goblin Rocket Fuel Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94265","cats":["crafting"]},"94345":{"id":94345,"t":"Craftsmans writ volcanic breastplate","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Volcanic Breastplate\nVolcanic Breastplate","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Volcanic Breastplate, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Volcanic Breastplate Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94345","cats":["crafting"]},"7945":{"id":7945,"t":"Your Fortune Awaits You...","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Palemane Rock in Mulgore and seek out your fortune.\nSayge's Fortune #27\nProvided: Sayge's Fortune #27","desc":"\"Your fortune awaits you outside Palemane Rock.\"\nThe fortune Sayge handed you feels slightly warm to the touch. Grasping it firmly, you see an image of the Palemane Rock of Mulgore. Focusing closer in on the image, you see a tree stump that sits close to the cave entrance.","rew":"You will receive:\nMysterious Lockbox\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"This tree stump looks like the one from your vision.","done":"A quick search of the tree stump reveals a lockbox from within it! It would seem that you have found your fortune!","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":36.2,"y":64.5,"n":"Mysterious Tree Stump","e":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"98025":{"id":98025,"t":"Wanted jaivhanel","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find and slay the owl known as Jai'vhanel and take one of her feathers. The black owl was last seen north of the Ameth'Aran ruins near the mountain base. Report the death of Jai'vhanel to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.\nFeather of Jai'vhanel","desc":"Attention!\nA reward is being offered for the death of the owl \"Jai'vhanel\" also know as \"Swordfeather\".\nUnfortunately this owl has gone mad and has begun to attack travelers as they journey along the road near Auberdine.\nJai'vhanel was last seen north of the Ameth'Aran ruins near the mountain base. Bring back one of her jet black feathers as proof of her death.\nReward claims for this bounty should be claimed with Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.\nThe Auberdine Village Council","rew":"You will receive:\nSwordfeather Cloak\nExperience: 1,150\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Greetings ‹class› - what may the Sentinels assist you with today? Perhaps you are here to inquire about the bounty on Jai'vhanel?","done":"It is good to know that issue has been taken care of, but it saddens me that we could not find another way. Jai'vhanel had been somewhat of a guardian of this area for quite some time, and I am not sure what could have caused her decent into madness.\nRegardless, thank you for your service today, ‹class›. The roads to Auberdine are safe for travel once again.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.2,"y":44.2,"n":"WANTED: Murkdeep!","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.6,"y":43.4,"n":"Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"985":{"id":985,"t":"How Big a Threat?","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 8 Blackwood Pathfinders and 5 Windtalkers and return to Terenthis in Auberdine.\nBlackwood Pathfinder slain : 0/ 8\nBlackwood Windtalker slain : 0/ 5","desc":"You've already proven adept at scouting our enemy, ‹name›. Do you have what it takes to fight them as well?\nNot all adventurers prefer straightforward combat to the art of stealth and evasion.\nIf you think you're up for the task, then the furbolg camp south of Auberdine is currently the biggest threat to our people. You'll find some of the Blackwood tribe there. Kill 8 pathfinders and 5 windtalkers, and return to me here.","rew":"Experience: 975\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Do not stay your hand from what must be done, child. I know how repulsive the idea of killing the creatures of the forest must be, but in this case it is necessary. No cure has been discovered for the corruption let loose upon the forest, and we must do what we can to halt its progress until one is found.","done":"Wash the blood from your garments, ‹name›, and do not mourn what you had to do. Instead, give thanks. You have lessened the threat to our people here in Auberdine, even if Darkshore is still in jeopardy from the effects of fel moss.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":39.4,"y":43.5,"n":"Terenthis","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"3785":{"id":3785,"t":"Morrowgrain Research","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use an Evergreen Pouch with a Packet of Tharlendis Seeds and two Un'Goro Soil samples to try and cultivate samples of Morrowgrain.\nBring 10 Morrowgrain to Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus.\n10 Morrowgrain\nProvided: Evergreen Pouch","desc":"Here's your Evergreen Pouch that you'll need to use the Tharlendis seeds with. You also need to have Un'Goro soil samples on hand to use as fertilizer for the seeds. Just use the pouch when you have everything; the pouch will take care of the rest.\nWhen you have enough morrowgrain, bring them here to me in the enclave. Please don't bother the Arch Druid; he's a very busy man, and he doesn't need to be disturbed every time someone returns with another batch of morrowgrain!","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Circle Cache\nExperience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Yes ‹name›, have you grown some morrowgrain for the Arch Druid's important research? The mysterious properties of Un'Goro Crater become clearer with each passing day, thanks to the help you are giving us.","done":"Well done ‹name›, I will be sure to give these to the Arch Druid himself when he has need of them. Meanwhile, please accept this as a token of the Cenarion Circle's appreciation.\nOur need for morrowgrain, for now, is constant; if you wish to continue aiding us, then please return when you have cultivated more of it.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"1465":{"id":1465,"t":"Vahlarriel's Search","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Malem Pendant to Vahlarriel Demonslayer in Desolace.\nMalem Pendant\nProvided: Malem Pendant","desc":"As you continue your search of the wagon you find not only a pendant, but also footprints leading off towards the south. In the distance you can see smoke rising from a large fort. The smoke is from a kept fire, not the burning of buildings, and your instincts tell you that the Malems, if still alive, were taken that direction.\nYou think Vahlarriel at Nijel's Point should not only see the pendant you've found, but also know about the signs of life to the south.","rew":"Experience: 1,950\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Infuriating! This entire fiasco!\nThe two of them were warned about how dangerous coming here would be. Now they're both missing... or worse.\nYou said you saw tracks heading to a fort nearby? That may be our best bet.\nFrom what the locals have said, that fortress is infested with members of the Burning Blade--orcs who have dedicated themselves to demon causes. They may not represent the majority of the Horde's beliefs, but they are evil and will slay you on sight if you're caught spying.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":56.5,"y":17.8,"n":"Malem Chest","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":66.4,"y":11.8,"n":"Vahlarriel Demonslayer","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"1385":{"id":1385,"t":"Brutal Politics","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nReach 3000 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur","desc":"Desolace is a land at war. The centaurs wage war with each other, and we believe the victor among them will spill out and threaten our strongholds. That, we cannot allow\nWe must learn how to beat the centaurs, and to do that... we must ally with one of the clans. The Magram centaurs war with the Gelkis. If you fight the Gelkis then the Magram might consider an alliance.\nEarn the favor of the Magrams then speak with Warug, in the Magram village in southeastern Desolace.","rew":"Experience: 2,050\n+100 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\n-500 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur","back":"You will go now, or the Magram will crush you! To be our friend, you must kill Gelkis.","done":"Many Gelkis fall to you. I like that. Maybe you can do more things I like. Maybe you and the Magram can be friends.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":66.7,"y":10.9,"n":"Captain Pentigast","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":75,"y":68.2,"n":"Warug","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"93225":{"id":93225,"t":"Carved centaur totems","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Acquire 5 Carved Centaur Totems by slaying centaur of any clan throughout Desolace, then return them to Gurda Wildmane at Ghost Walker Post.\n5 Carved Centaur Totem","desc":"I have noticed that centaur from different clans sometimes gather away from settlements and engage in trade. I have observed this across numerous nights and seemingly with every clan; most importantly I have seen the currency they use: carved totems.\nI believe we can turn the tides in our favor with either the Gelkis or the Magram if we deliver a heavy bundle of totems right to them. I have already begun carving some, but I doubt they will be easily fooled without a few authentic ones.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":56.2,"y":59.6,"n":"Gurda Wildmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"93465":{"id":93465,"t":"Notes on draenethyst","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Take Gimashi's notes on Draenethyst, and bring them back to Azore Aldamort.\nGimashi's Findings","desc":"I suppose it would be more accurate to say I know someone who knows a thing or two about draenethyst.\nYou see, the warlocks of the Burning Blade have been studying it. It is a substance from beyond the dark portal, so it follows that those involved with darker arts might wish to harness it to their own ends. We cannot allow this, obviously.\nThe specific warlock you seek is named Gimashi. She can be found atop her tower, which is in a ravine to the southeast. Her notes will have the answers you seek.","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,150\nLevel 40 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 36 38 43 51 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 93465\nThe chain\n2 quests from level 38 to 40, 3,850 XP in all.\n1 [ 38 ] The Visiting Mage\nFind the mage in Desolace who knows about the power of draenethyst.\n700 XP\n2 [ 40 ] Notes on Draenethyst this quest\nTake Gimashi's notes on Draenethyst, and bring them back to Azore Aldamort.\n3,150 XP","cats":["desolace"]},"96825":{"id":96825,"t":"This fruit could bite back","lv":6,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Cook Torka in Razor Hill wants you to collect 8 Prickly Pear Fruit from the Razormane Grounds west of town.\n8 Prickly Pear Fruit","desc":"Our hunters and fishers bring back plenty of savory food for our troops - but it's rare that they get a sweet treat.\nI've seen a cactus that produces a prickly, tasty fruit. But it only grows in the hills to the west, where the wretched quilboars make their camps. Make your way past the quilboars and bring me some of those fruits. And be careful - the fruits are as spiny as the quilboars!","rew":"Money: 1 0 gold, 1 silver, 0 copper Experience: 410\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Did you find the fruits?","done":"I'll use these to prepare something tasty, and save the seeds for planting. Someday we'll have prickly pears growing all around Orgrimmar!","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":51.2,"y":42.4,"n":"Cook Torka","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"825":{"id":825,"t":"From The Wreckage....","lv":8,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gar'Thok of Razor Hill wants you to retrieve 3 Gnomish Tools from the wreckage off the coast.\n3 Gnomish Tools Gnomish Toolbox","desc":"One of my most observant scouts brings back word that the wreckage of Proudmoore's fleet still remains off the coast of Durotar, just east of Tiragarde Keep.\nIt is no secret that the humans, in alliance with those foul little creatures known as gnomes, have an advanced knowledge of mechanics. We must have a complete understanding of all our potential enemies. And our people will benefit from this new knowledge as well.\nSwim through the wreckage, ‹name›, and retrieve for me the tools of the Alliance.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDirt-trodden Boots Sandrunner Wristguards Wide Metal Girdle\nExperience: 700\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Once we learn how the humans operate their strange machinery, we will stand a greater chance of defeating them in future battles.\nWith our new gained knowledge, the Horde only stands to grow in strength.","done":"Your recovery mission was a success, ‹class›. I will see to it that these tools get to Orgrimmar with the next caravan.\nNicely done.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":51.9,"y":43.5,"n":"Gar'Thok","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"97225":{"id":97225,"t":"Forgotten loa idols","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 8 Forgotten Loa Idols from the Echo Isles. Bring them to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village.\n8 Forgotten Loa Idol","desc":"When we fled the isles that Zalazane and his ilk now inhabit, we left behind many precious idols that help us commune with spirits we worship: our loa. They are of grave importance to our tribe.\nThe followers of Zalazane show no reverence for our loa and have scattered these idols across the largest of the isles.\nThis is an action that will not go unnoticed if we are not able to collect these idols, and offending a loa is a grave matter.\nGo, find as many loa idols as you can and return them to me.","rew":"You will receive:\nDepleted Ritual Band\nExperience: 775\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Have you found our loa idols, Enve? We must begin our rituals again soon.","done":"You have done a great deed for our tribe today.\nUnlike some tribes, our kinship with our loa is one of reverence and respect, and we owe them much.\nI would not want the Darkspear to fall out of favor with them.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":55.8,"y":74.4,"n":"Master Vornal","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":56,"y":74.6,"n":"Master Gadrin","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"265":{"id":265,"t":"The Shadowy Search Continues","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"See if other townsfolk have clues about the shadowy figure.\nBook from Sven's Farm\nProvided: Book from Sven's Farm","desc":"Here is your book back, ‹name›, and I bid you fortune with your search. If you ask others in town, perhaps they can offer you more clues.\nAnd here is one more for you - although the author of this book is a stranger to Darkshire, the book itself was purchased here.","rew":"Experience: 200","back":"Sometimes I'll sell blank books to scholars and mages, or to anyone who wants to keep a journal.\nI remember well everyone to whom I sold a book within the last few months...","done":"Ah, yes. I sold this book a month ago to a shady person. He didn't tell me his name, but he was a nervous, jittery chap, always looking over his shoulder.\nI hope that helps you...","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":45.3,"n":"Madame Eva","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.5,"y":46.9,"n":"Clerk Daltry","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"6585":{"id":6585,"t":"The Test of Skulls, Axtroz","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Grim Batol and track down Axtroz, drake champion of the Red Flight. Destroy him and take his skull. Return the skull to Emberstrife.\nThe Skull of Axtroz Axtroz","desc":"It was over the mountains of Grim Batol that our Father raged against the combined might of the Aspects. The cowardly act of the betrayer, Alexstrasza, bought the other Aspects enough time to escape from Father's wrath.\nSssuch a shameful act...\nThe Red Flight now guards Grim Batol, their lieutenant, Axtroz, must be destroyed. Return the skull of Axtroz to me. For Father, whelp!","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Changesss... I sense them taking place in you, whelp. Pass this test and only ceremony remains.","done":"I had doubted your dedication, whelp. You persisted, dominating our enemies, bringing honor to our flight.\nI must now prepare the skulls for your ascension.\nDustwallow Marsh Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":56.7,"y":87.7,"n":"Emberstrife","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5065":{"id":5065,"t":"The Lost Tablets of Mosh'aru","lv":58,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Third and Fourth Mosh'aru Tablets to Prospector Ironboot in Tanaris.\nThird Mosh'aru Tablet Third Mosh'aru Tablet\nFourth Mosh'aru Tablet Fourth Mosh'aru Tablet","desc":"The troll with whom you spoke did not tell the truth. The two tablets you gained for him spoke of containing the essence of Hakkar, but there is more to that legend. I have studied long, and found that there are six Tablets of Mosh'aru, not two! Six!\nAnd I fear that we will not like what secrets the others hold..\nFind the third and fourth tablets of Mosh'aru. They're in the Eastern Plaguelands, held by the mossflayer trolls. Find them, and bring them to me.","rew":"Experience: 7,750","back":"Do you have the tablets? I fear their texts will reveal a great threat to our world.","done":"You found them! Great!\nThank you, ‹name›. I will pour over these texts and decipher their meaning.\nYou, however, have another task...\nTanaris Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":66.9,"y":24,"n":"Prospector Ironboot","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9225":{"id":9225,"t":"Epic Armaments of Battle - Revered Amongst the Dawn","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"For 45 Insignias of the Dawn and 45 Insignias of the Crusade you may choose an item from the Argent Dawn's treasure cache.\n45 Insignia of the Dawn\n45 Insignia of the Crusade","desc":"Greetings, friend. Have you insignias of the Dawn or the Crusade that you would like to redeem for items of great power?\nI must warn you; epic purchases made at revered reputation with the Dawn are still quite expensive. I would advise that you gain a better reputation with the Dawn before moving forward with your plans.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAmulet of the Dawn Bracers of Hope Bracers of Subterfuge Medallion of the Dawn Talisman of Ascendance The Purifier\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Choose carefully. There are no refunds.","done":"Good day, ‹name›. It was a pleasure doing business with you.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.8,"y":50.2,"n":"Quartermaster Miranda Breechlock","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"6185":{"id":6185,"t":"The Eastern Plagues","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Scour the Eastern Plaguelands for clues as to the \"Blightcaller\" and the missing SI:7 agents. If you find any SI:7 Insignias, return them to Flint Shadowmore at Chillwind Camp.\nSI:7 Insignia (Rutger) Mangled Human Remains\nSI:7 Insignia (Fredo) Mangled Human Remains\nSI:7 Insignia (Turyen) Mangled Human Remains","desc":"As I said, your first mission is one of reconnaissance. Nothing fancy, ‹name›. You must travel to the Eastern Plaguelands and look for any clues as to this Blightcaller.\nBe on the lookout for information about our missing operatives. We have to assume that they are dead and if they are dead, they must have a corpse... somewhere.\n<Flint swallows hard.>\nAll SI:7 agents carry this insignia.\n<Flint shows you his SI:7 insignia.>\nBring any of those that you may find back to me.","rew":"Experience: 8,300","back":"An... Any luck??","done":"Rutger. Fredo. Turyen. All... dead...\n<Flint clutches the insignias tightly.>\nWhere were they? Did you discover any more information about this bastard, the Blightcaller?\nWestern Plaguelands Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43.6,"y":84.5,"n":"Flint Shadowmore","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"5545":{"id":5545,"t":"A Bundle of Trouble","lv":9,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Bundles of Wood to Raelen at the Eastvale Logging Camp.\n8 Bundle of Wood Bundle of Wood","desc":"I've got a real problem on my hands. I have a deadline looming for an order of lumber, and I'm running out of time. The wolves and bears north of here have chased my workers away from the bundles of wood that they've already chopped.\nI've already talked to Deputy Rainer about clearing the animals, but I need someone to go collect the wood for me. If you could collect eight bundles of wood for me I might just make my deadline.","rew":"Money: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 775","back":"That deadline isn't getting any further away, ‹class›. Please hurry and collect those bundles of wood.","done":"Excellent! Thanks to you, I should be able to complete the order in time. To show my gratitude, I would like to offer some coin as compensation for your troubles.\nThank you and farewell.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":81.4,"y":66.1,"n":"Supervisor Raelen","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"4505":{"id":4505,"t":"Well of Corruption","lv":54,"min":49,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,450 experience instead of 5,400, 1.01 times as much.","obj":"Collect a sample of corrupted water from the Jadefire Satyrs' moonwell and bring it to Winna Hazzard at Bloodvenom Post.\nFilled Flasket\nProvided: Hardened Flasket","desc":"Some may say that I am exceptionally cruel... But truly, it is only a strong desire to see the Horde gain an advantage against the Alliance, in any way possible.\nMy newest interest is a moonwell at the Ruins of Constellas, south of here, tended by the Jadefire satyrs. The moonwell, once a symbol of renewal for the insufferable night elves, is now corrupted, and used to bring forth more satyrs.\nI have an idea, ‹name›, and I'd like a sample of the water... for my little feline friend here.","rew":"Experience: 5,450\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"This is of utmost importance. Be on your way, now.","done":"Very well. We must find a way to use this corruption against our enemies...","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":34.2,"y":52.3,"n":"Winna Hazzard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4105":{"id":4105,"t":"Salve via Gathering","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Fel Creep Sungrass 15 % , Mountain Silversage 15 % , Dreamfoil 15 % , Golden Sansam 15 % and 3 more","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"A Cenarion beacon allows a seasoned herbalist to spot insidious fel creep - a malfeasant product of Felwood's corruption. My work here has taught me the knowledge of purifying fel creep into a cleansing reagent... used in what we now refer to as Cenarion plant salve.\nWhen you gather herbs in Felwood, you should encounter the fel creep so long as you have the beacon. In exchange for what you bring to me, I will give you pre-made Cenarion plant salve.","done":"Excellent work ‹name› - every bit of this, once we purify it, will help us take back Felwood. Here, take some doses of Cenarion plant salve and head into the forest. The reclaiming of the land from the corruption waits for no ‹race›!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":54.1,"y":86.8,"n":"Arathandris Silversky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"5385":{"id":5385,"t":"The Remains of Trey Lightforge","lv":57,"min":49,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Remains of Trey Lightforge to Jessir Moonbow in Felwood.\nRemains of Trey Lightforge\nProvided: Remains of Trey Lightforge","desc":"You pick up the sack carefully and prepare to make your way back to Jessir Moonbow on the border of Felwood and Ashenvale. Hopefully the paladin will be given the proper respects once you've passed his remains on to his friends.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHunt Tracker Blade Tidecrest Blade\nMoney: 22 0 gold, 22 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,550","back":"How did things go in Jaedenar, ‹name›?","done":"You've done it! Praise be to Elune and whichever powers you worshihp, ‹name›. You have done an honorable and noble thing this day. I am certain Arko'narin will be pleased that you not only took the time to save her, but to also slay the creature who tortured one of her best friends.\nI wish I could do more for you, but please, take this.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":38.5,"y":50.4,"n":"Remains of Trey Lightforge","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":51.3,"y":82,"n":"Jessir Moonbow","e":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4265":{"id":4265,"t":"Freed from the Hive","lv":46,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Free Raschal from the Zukk'ash hive.\nReturn to Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon Stronghold and let him know that Raschal is alive and well.","desc":"The pod splits opens some when you touch it, revealing a night elven male who is surprisingly still alive. He seems to be in good health, though deeply stunned. As you help him down from the pod, he stirs to life.\n\"Thank Elune - you've saved me, friend! I... I'm Raschal, and I awoke paralyzed inside this pod after these bugs overwhelmed me. Were you sent by the Stronghold?\"\nIt would seem that you've found the missing courier!","rew":"Experience: 4,050\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"You have something to report, ‹name›?","done":"Welcome home, ‹name›. Raschal checked in just a little while ago and told me what happened.\nI... no, the entire Stronghold can't even begin to thank you for your great deed; Raschal would have been dead without your timely aid, and your assistance came to us without even so much as the whisper of a mercenary's fee. You bear the mark of a true hero. Know that you will always have a friend in Ginro Hearthkindle.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":72.1,"y":63.7,"n":"Zukk'ash Pod","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":31.9,"y":45.1,"n":"Ginro Hearthkindle","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"97065":{"id":97065,"t":"Tip the scales keefers angelfish","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Keefer's Angelfish","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Speckled Tastyfish\nLevel 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 97065","cats":["fishing"]},"8905":{"id":8905,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Wildheart Bracers to Deliana in Ironforge.\n15 Winterspring Blood Sample Rabid Shardtooth 30 % , Elder Shardtooth 30 % , Shardtooth Bear 30 % , Shardtooth Mauler 30 % and 4 more\nWildheart Bracers Wailing Banshee 4.6 % in Stratholme , Crimson Inquisitor 4.5 % , Shrieking Banshee 3.9 % in Stratholme , Diseased Ghoul 1.4 % in Scholomance","desc":"Well met, ‹class›. I've something that might interest you.\nI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality. I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.\nThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment. Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold. You shall find the effort worth your while.","rew":"You will receive:\nFeralheart Bracers\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you brought me what I requested of you, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent! Let's perform the trade then. It's hard to part with this excellent armor, but I'm afraid I won't be needing it any time soon.\nIf you're interested in performing more work for me, I might be willing to give up the rest of the pieces.\nDun Morogh Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"5145":{"id":5145,"t":"Dragonscale Leatherworking","lv":55,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 2 Tough Scorpid Breastplates, 2 Tough Scorpid Gloves, and 10 Worn Dragonscales to Thorkaf Dragoneye in the Badlands.\nCompleting this quest will give you access to the Dragonscale Leatherworking arts.\nThe completion of this quest will prevent you from learning Elemental Leatherworking and Tribal Leatherworking; be sure this is the path you wish to follow before doing so.\n2 Tough Scorpid Breastplate\n2 Tough Scorpid Gloves\n10 Worn Dragonscale Jademir Oracle 2.4 % , Dreamstalker 2.2 % , Verdantine Oracle 2 % , Verdantine Boughguard 1.9 %","desc":"Dragonscale leatherworking isn't easy, but it's extremely rewarding. I'll teach you how to make this fine mail armor, but only if you agree to certain conditions.\nBy choosing this path, you agree never to learn elemental or tribal leatherworking; there is only room for one of the three at the apex of the craft. Furthermore, I'll need some samples of your best work involving scorpid armor. Finally, I'll need proof of your ability to acquire the staple of the trade: scales of the dragonkin.","rew":"You will learn: Dragonscale Leatherworking\nExperience: 4,200\n+200 reputation with Leatherworking - Dragonscale","back":"If you're ready to commit to a permanent decision by becoming a dragonscale leatherworker, then I'm ready to take you on as a student. Just bring to me the things I asked for, and we'll begin your education.","done":"I'll hand it to you - it takes a strong will to make a permanent decision like you've just done. I assure you, dragonscale leatherworking will prove to be a profitable and rewarding path for you to follow.\nTo train in the art for the future, simply speak to me and I will make available any knowledge that you have yet to commit as yours.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":62.7,"y":57.4,"n":"Thorkaf Dragoneye","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"7785":{"id":7785,"t":"Examine the Vessel","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Examine the Vessel of Rebirth and return it to Highlord Demitrian.\nVessel of Rebirth\nProvided: Vessel of Rebirth","desc":"Examine the vessel of his rebirth, mortal. It is from this that the Windseeker shall be reborn!","back":"Will you release him from his eternal prison?","done":"May you be protected in your crusade. May the Master bless your efforts.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":21.7,"y":8.6,"n":"Highlord Demitrian","e":1}],"cats":["legendary"]},"86585":{"id":86585,"t":"Banner of the fallen","lv":17,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Raise the standard of Ironforge, call out the trogg Headsplitter and kill it, then report to Captain Rugelfuss.\nHeadsplitter slain\nProvided: Banner of Ironforge","desc":"The fallen mountaineer bears a standard of Ironforge. Perhaps she was scouting, or making a doomed charge. Either way, the standard has been cast down and trampled. The mountaineer was hit on the head so hard that her helm was knocked off and she was killed outright by a trogg, likely with a spiked club.\nThe trogg that killed her is probably still nearby, and likely remembers the banner. Raising the banner of Ironforge once more may call it out.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMountaineer's Greataxe Invader's Mace\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,250\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"That banner looks like it's been in a war!","done":"You found Ylva's body? Ah, the poor woman. She said she was going to show the troggs that Ironforge would never fall to their kind. She went looking for a few mountaineers who never returned from a patrol through trogg country. She was always too independent-minded to be cautious. Now we know what happened.\nI'll take the banner back and make sure it's cleaned up and displayed. You should take her weapon. May it serve you well against the troggs.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":31.8,"y":86.2,"n":"Mountaineer Ylva","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":23.2,"y":73.8,"n":"Captain Rugelfuss","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"1945":{"id":1945,"t":"Laughing Sisters","lv":26,"min":26,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 12 Laughing Sister's Hairs to Kil'hala at the Crossroads.\n12 Laughing Sister's Hair Laughing Sister","desc":"For your services, I have arranged for the creation of your new robes, provided you can gather the needed materials...\nFor these robes, you must return to Ashenvale for the locks of hair from laughing sisters--dryads who gather near the Raynewood Retreat.\nWhen you have their hair, bring it to Kil'hala, a troll tailor at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He will be expecting you, and will fashion your robes.","rew":"Experience: 1,600","back":"Greetings, ‹name›. Deino said you would come, and would bring the laughing sisters' hair. Do you have it?","done":"Ah, this hair will weave into a fine robe, ‹name›. It is a pity the laughing sisters had to die to part with it, though I do doubt they would ever give it willingly.\nA pity, but only a small one.\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.4,"y":86.1,"n":"Deino","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.2,"y":31.7,"n":"Kil'hala","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"7065":{"id":7065,"t":"Corruption of Earth and Seed","lv":51,"min":45,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Princess Theradras and return to Keeper Marandis at Nijel's Point in Desolace.\nPrincess Theradras slain","desc":"In the depths of Maraudon lives a creature of chaos and evil, ‹name›. Princess Theradras is an elemental force of earth related somehow to the Old Gods. Ages ago, she was sought out by Zaetar, first son of Cenarius. The offspring of their... relationship are the creatures known as centaur. Ever-thankful creatures, the centaur killed Zaetar, and now Theradras keeps his remains. My quest here is to find those powerful enough to slay Theradras so we may recover Zaetar's remains before returning to Stonetalon.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nThrash Blade Resurgence Rod Verdant Keeper's Aim\nExperience: 6,100\n+150 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"I feel the weight of imposing my plea on the mortal races, but we are left with no other options. The races of Azeroth have proven without a doubt they can overcome such things when they work together, so it is to them I ask for help.\nI only hope it is enough.\nZaetar, brother to Remulos, brought many pains to this world, and ultimately it caused his own death. There is a lesson there to all of us if we are wise enough to see it.","done":"This is most wonderful news, ‹name›! Thank you!\nAlthough it concerns me that you were not able to bring back Zaetar's remains, who am I to question the will of Cenarius' first born. Perhaps now the will of the centaur will break and their thirst for blood will lesson--we can only hope.\nIf successful in our mission, I was given these items to reward any who aided us. You may choose one as a token of thanks.\nDesolace Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":63.8,"y":10.7,"n":"Keeper Marandis","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["maraudon"]},"745":{"id":745,"t":"Sharing the Land","lv":8,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 8 instead of 6. Pays 2s 25c instead of 1s 25c. Gives 700 experience instead of 550, 1.27 times as much.","obj":"Kill 10 Palemane Tanners, 8 Palemane Skinners, and 5 Palemane Poachers, then return to Baine Bloodhoof in Bloodhoof Village.\nPalemane Tanner slain : 0/ 10\nPalemane Skinner slain : 0/ 8\nPalemane Poacher slain : 0/ 5","desc":"‹name›, there are many conflicts that wound this land. It is my hope that you will not bear witness to as many of them as I have. Yet there is one that I would ask you to seek out. It will give you some sense of how terrible, if left unchecked, even a small threat can be to the land.\nPalemane gnolls have settled to the south of Bloodhoof and in a cave to the west. They disrespect our attempts to communicate with them, and they slay the wildlife of Mulgore unbridled.\nWords are no longer the answer.","rew":"You will receive:\n25 Flash Pellet\nMoney: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 700\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"If the Palemanes had respected the land and its inhabitants more, this conflict would have never occurred.","done":"‹name›, it is good you've taken my task seriously. Respect of the land and its creatures is important. Death and life are a circle... a necessity. One cannot exist without the other. Take time to ponder this and do well to never forget it.\nMulgore Shen'dralas","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.7,"y":63.4,"n":"Baine Bloodhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"1785":{"id":1785,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":13,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Tiza Battleforge in Ironforge.","desc":"I c'n see me wife's o'er there beamin' wit pride already. Ya better get yer tuchus o'er there pronto. I be thinkin' she'd have some words wit ya.\nLight be witcha, mighty ‹class›. I'll be lookin' fer ya on the battlefield against the Scourge and dem Dark Irons when the time comes.","rew":"You will learn: Redemption\nExperience: 1,150","done":"You've done all of Ironforge a great favor today, ‹name›. I'm proud to count you among us, and if you feel you're ready, I would like to bless you with this scroll. The Symbol of Life would only have worked when used by a ‹class› who was ready for one of the Light's greatest blessings-the power to restore the dead back to life.\nI will teach you the ability to resurrect your companions. Use it wisely, ‹name›, and thank you, on behalf of myself, my husband, and Ironforge.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54.9,"y":22.4,"n":"Muiredon Battleforge","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":23,"n":"Tiza Battleforge","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5625":{"id":5625,"t":"Garments of the Light","lv":4,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Mountaineer Dolf and heal his wounds using Lesser Heal (Rank 2). Afterwards, grant him Power Word: Fortitude and then return to Maxan Anvol in Kharanos.\nHeal and fortify Mountaineer Dolf","desc":"It's usually about this time that one of your power is tested to see if they're worthy of wearing robes denoting their place in the church. But to be honest, I got more pressing matters to look into. Citizen of Kharanos' just came in here and told me 'bout a hurt mountaineer just outside town to the south--name's Dolf.\nYou heal Dolf and give him Fortitude, and I'll consider you done with proving yourself. How's that sound?","rew":"You will receive:\nFriar's Robes of the Light\nExperience: 270","back":"Have you found Dolf yet, ‹name›?\nYou've probably already learned this, but our ability to heal is very useful. Not only are we able to take care of the wounded, but we're vital to the survival of all those would-be heroes out there trying to make a name for themselves. With Fortitude to increase the amount of blows we can take, and our healing magic to keep them alive, there's nothing we can't overcome!","done":"Excellent, ‹name›. With one more healthy guard out there to help the town, we'll be that much safer. I'm glad to see you're already learning to use your abilities wisely. If you feel you are ready for more training at any time, please come back to me. But for now, take this robe. It will let others know that you are one of our order. If you don't want to wear it, that's fine. Later there will be more tests and this robe isn't necessary for those.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.3,"y":52.2,"n":"Maxan Anvol","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"94825":{"id":94825,"t":"Confounding flash","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.","desc":"Just a short time ago, one of your priests was here looking for you, ‹race›. He said that if I were to see you, I should direct you towards the Hall of Mysteries. He said it was very important, but I would not be overly concerned if I were you. His demeanor seemed positive... as though it were good news. I wouldn't take too long in making my way there if I were you.\nElune be with you, good ‹race›.\nLevel 10 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 13 16 Side Alliance Class Priest Shareable Yes Quest ID 94825","cats":["priest"]},"8825":{"id":8825,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Horde Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with Thunder Bluff. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.\nOrgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":33,"y":71.6,"n":"Thunder Bluff Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":42.4,"y":57,"n":"Officer Thunderstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"99145":{"id":99145,"t":"A winter veil gift","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","rew":"You will receive:\nA Winter Veil Gift\nLevel 1 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 4 6 Side Both factions Quest ID 99145","cats":["seasonal"]},"2985":{"id":2985,"t":"Call of Water","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Islen Waterseer in the Barrens.","desc":"You look ready for your next test, ‹name›. You've been patient in your studies, but the time has come for you to learn more. The time has come for you to learn about the purity of water.\nSeek out Islen Waterseer in the Barrens. She is along the eastern coast, south of the Southfury River and Ratchet. You will find her there at her fishing hut. Good luck to you, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 775","done":"The wind approaches you quickly from the horizon; the earth is steady beneath your feet; and your spirit is already warmed by fire--I would say it is time for you to learn about the purity of water.\nYour path has led you this far, and your spirit will give you the strength to carry on even further. But the first step is yours to take.\nDurotar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":54.4,"y":42.6,"n":"Swart","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":65.8,"y":43.8,"n":"Islen Waterseer","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"94505":{"id":94505,"t":"Call of water","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Shard of Water to Norric Lochthane in Loch Modan.\nProvided: Shard of Water","desc":"Take shard. Take shard and give life.\nGive life and understand. Understand water is life... corruption stops life.\nYou protect and give life with water's power.","rew":"You will receive:\nWater Totem\nExperience: 2,750","back":"How fared your journey to Westfall? Success there is hard to measure, but even small victories carry weight.","done":"Aye, this is the proof I asked for, and ye've done well, Theinn. I'm proud to be the first to offer my congratulations--and yer water totem. Use it wisely, and may fortune walk beside ye.\nYer next trial won't come soon, so take this time to learn. Pure water heals, aye, but its gifts go far beyond mending wounds.\nSilverpine Forest Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":38.6,"y":44.6,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Water","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":41.8,"y":19,"n":"Norric Lochthane","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8745":{"id":8745,"t":"Treasure of the Timeless One","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFang of Korialstrasz Shadowsong's Sorrow Runesword of the Red Ravencrest's Legacy\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":25.9,"y":91,"n":"Jonathan the Revelator","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"425":{"id":425,"t":"Ivar the Foul","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Ivar the Foul, and bring Ivar's Head to Rane Yorick at the Ivar Patch.\nIvar's Head Ivar the Foul","desc":"My brother Quinn and I were tasked to recon Silverpine Forest and report to High Executor Hadrec. But we didn't get far -- when moving through this farm we were attacked by the ghoul Ivar the Foul.\nWe escaped from Ivar, but he seriously mauled Quinn. He's healing from the potion you gave him, but Ivar may return before Quinn recovers.\nKill Ivar so Quinn will have time to heal. Ivar is usually in the barn yonder, waiting for my guard to drop.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nQuilted Bracers Weathered Belt\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 675\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you killed Ivar the Foul? If you won't do it for me and my brother, then do it for the Forsaken.","done":"Ah, thank you. You have my gratitude, ‹name›.\nAnd I will include you in the report I make to my superiors.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":53.5,"y":13.4,"n":"Rane Yorick","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"95065":{"id":95065,"t":"Fishin time","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 1 Shiny Bauble and 3 Nightcrawlers to Gilbert Gray at the harbor in Stormwind.\nShiny Bauble\n3 Nightcrawlers","desc":"What a view... Best an old man can ask for.\nThe fish sure are bitin' now, though I'm down to my last bait. I don't suppose you have any spare fishing supplies on you? Of course not, forgive me. I get so excited at the thought of casting another line it didn't dawn on me I may be one of the few carrying supplies everywhere I go.\nWould you be able to help refresh my stock? Catherine Leland has an assortment of fishing goods just west of the Trade District along the canals. Tell her old Gray sent you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Brilliant Smallfish 5 Rainbow Fin Albacore\nMoney: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900","back":"Did you get the fishing supplies?","done":"Great timing! Caught a big one with my last bait. Great day so far. They're really biting out here!\nTell you what, since you were kind enough to keep this old man in business how about a few fish for the road?","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":26.2,"y":47,"n":"Gilbert Gray","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"345":{"id":345,"t":"Ink Supplies","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Foreman Oslow in Lakeshire and ask him for Rethban Iron Ore.","desc":"I've been meaning to finish my copy of The Stresses of Iron, but...\nWell you see, I make my own ink for books I copy. It's my own recipe; it doesn't run or smear, and it dries very quickly Unfortunately, it dries too quickly! My last batch dried up before I could finish the copying job, and I haven't had the chance to make more ink!\nTo make more I need Rethban Iron Ore from the Redridge Mountains. Foreman Oslow in Lakeshire is my usual supplier.","rew":"Experience: 490\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"You need what?? Maybe you haven't noticed, but we're busy fortifying Lakeshire's defenses and repairing damage from recent orc attacks. If you need Rethban Iron Ore, you'll have to get it yourself!\nElwynn Forest Redridge Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.6,"y":40.4,"n":"Brother Paxton","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":27.1,"y":48.6,"n":"Foreman Oslow","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"2745":{"id":2745,"t":"Infiltrating the Castle","lv":31,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Tyrion in Stormwind Castle.","desc":"Hmm, an interesting tale, and not one to be taken lightly. Yeah, I can help you, but what you need to do is divvy out a form of justice that's not... legal, if you're to see this through to the end.\nLescovar and Marzon need to be dealt with, and swiftly. Do you think you're capable of such a thing?\nYou decide. If so, then make haste to the castle and find an old friend of mine, a gnome named Tyrion. He's been watching Lescovar now for a couple weeks. He should be able to help you end this.","rew":"Experience: 250","done":"What the...?! Don't sneak up on me like that! And keep your voice down! What in the name of the Shadow are you doing sneakin' up on me for? Can't you see I'm busy, you daft fool?\nWhat do you mean, what am I doing? I'm waiting for the next Dark Portal to open, what the heck do you think I'm doing? Speak your peace and be off with you... 'fore the guards notice the two of us hiding in the bushes together. I have a reputation to maintain.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":66,"y":74.1,"n":"Elling Trias","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":73.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Tyrion","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"185":{"id":185,"t":"Tiger Mastery","lv":31,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Ajeck Rouack of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to kill 10 Young Stranglethorn Tigers.\nYoung Stranglethorn Tiger slain : 0/ 10","desc":"When I was but a young girl, my father trained me in the art of tiger hunting.\nYou'll find the young felines much easier to track and slay. For this reason, we'll start you out easy. One can often find young tigers near the expedition camp.\nTest your tracking skills and see if you can hunt some of the beasts down.","rew":"Experience: 1,250","back":"I don't feel confident in training you further, ‹name›, until you have proven yourself skilled in slaying the youngest of the tigers first.","done":"Nicely done, ‹name›. You are ready to move on.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.6,"y":10.6,"n":"Ajeck Rouack","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"585":{"id":585,"t":"Speaking with Nezzliok","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Balia'mah Trophy, a Ziata'jai Trophy and a Zul'Mamwe Trophy to the Bubbling Cauldron at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\nBalia'mah Trophy Balia'mah Trophy Skulls\nZiata'jai Trophy Ziata'jai Trophy Skulls\nZul'Mamwe Trophy Zul'Mamwe Trophy Skulls","desc":"<The head of Nezzliok speaks.>\nIt is true. I know where the child of the Darkspears was taken. You have bested me and bound my spirit, but I will say nothing without appeasement!\nThe Bloodscalps war with the Skullsplitters. To gain my favor, steal from the Skullsplitters 3 of their trophy skulls and place them here with us, so that my spirit will have slaves in the Nether. One skull must be from their trophy pile in Balia'mah, another from Ziata'jai, and the last from Zul'Mamwe.","rew":"Experience: 2,350\n+75 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"I await the skulls...","done":"Yes. These will serve me well. When my spirit is freed, I will enter the Nether with three fine servants!\nYou are a credit to your ‹race› clan, and you have appeased me.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.2,"y":27.6,"n":"Bubbling Cauldron","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"3625":{"id":3625,"t":"Enchanted Azsharite Fel Weaponry","lv":58,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Wait for Galvan to finish forging the weaponry.","desc":"‹name›, the creation of each weapon will take some time.\nAdditionally, you may only use the power of the Felcurse once per three minutes. Its weakening properties against Razelikh the Defiler and his minions may be variable in duration. This is why you must release the Felcurse only when the moment is right!\nNow give me a moment to craft your weapon, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEnchanted Azsharite Felbane Dagger Enchanted Azsharite Felbane Staff Enchanted Azsharite Felbane Sword\nExperience: 625","back":"To interrupt the forging process could result in an imperfect weapon. Be patient, ‹name›.","done":"<Galvan wipes the sweat from his brow.>\nA finer demon slayer has never existed, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":50.6,"y":20.5,"n":"Galvan the Ancient","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"3385":{"id":3385,"t":"The Undermarket","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 40 instead of 46. Gives 4,700 experience instead of 6,750, 0.7 times as much.","obj":"Slay Trade Master Kovic and his minion Clunk. Retrieve the Trader's Satchel from his corpse and return it to Nilith.\nTrader's Satchel Trade Master Kovic\nTrade Master Kovic slain\nClunk slain","desc":"They call themselves the Undermarket: Cutthroat traders that will sell, move, trade and do just about anything for the right price.\nIt gets worse, ‹name›. They have set up a base of operations here in the Searing Gorge. Trade Master Kovic is heading up the operation and has close ties with the Dark Iron dwarves of the region.\nWe must strike hard and send a message to their leadership. Slay Trade Master Kovic and his minion Clunk. Bring back his trader's satchel when the job is done.\nTo the Cauldron!","rew":"You will receive:\nShadowy Belt Kovic's Trading Satchel\nExperience: 4,700","back":"The Trade Master still lives?","done":"You have struck a decisive blow against the Undermarket. Their leaders will think twice before sending more cronies into the gorge.\nOh, and I also found nothing of use in the trader's satchel. You may keep whatever you find inside.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":41,"y":74.9,"n":"Nilith Lokrav","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tailoring"]},"8585":{"id":8585,"t":"The Isle of Dread!","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Recover Lakmaeran's Carcass and 20 Chimaerok Tenderloins for Dirge Quikcleave in Tanaris.\nLakmaeran's Carcass Lord Lakmaeran\n20 Chimaerok Tenderloin Arcane Chimaerok 48.7 % , Chimaerok Devourer 47.4 % , Chimaerok 46 % , Lord Lakmaeran 23.9 %","desc":"Legend has it that the chimaerok of the Isle of Dread in Feralas have the most succulent and tender vittles in existence! Now these chimaerok also have a daddy who, with proper preparation, may or may not look like a 500 pound chicken.\nHead to the Isle of Dread and kill Lord Lakmaeran and bring me his fresh carcass. That should satisfy the gnome. To satisfy me, you'll need to get your hands on some chimaerok tenderloin.\nDo this and you'll have your 500 pound chicken and a little something extra.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Mmmmm... Chimaerok...","done":"Look at the marbleization on those tenderloins! Fantastic!\nNow about that chicken... Hrm, let me see. I'm going to need a few minutes to devise the recipe.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.6,"y":28.1,"n":"Dirge Quikcleave","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"905":{"id":905,"t":"The Angry Scytheclaws","lv":17,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Sunscale raptors and collect their feathers. Use the feathers on the 3 Scytheclaw nests. Return to Sergra Darkthorn in the Crossroads.\nVisit Blue Raptor Nest\nVisit Yellow Raptor Nest\nVisit Red Raptor Nest","desc":"Now, ‹name›, the hunt deepens. Now you must defeat your prey, and then find your way to its lair.\nHunt the sunscale raptors to the south. Slay them and remove the feathers they wear. Place the feathers on the scytheclaw nests southwest of the Stagnant Oasis. Show their brethren you do not fear them!","rew":"Money: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,250\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Have you been to the nests, ‹name›?","done":"So you've been to the nests and placed the feathers of your prey within them. That took a fair portion of courage, no doubt about it.\nDo you feel a little tougher, ‹name›? Because you look tougher now then when you first came here. I guess the Barrens is doing its job.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.2,"y":31,"n":"Sergra Darkthorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1145":{"id":1145,"t":"The Swarm Grows","lv":33,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Korran's Sealed Note to Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar.\nKorran's Sealed Note\nProvided: Korran's Sealed Note","desc":"Many travelers who've come through the Crossroads helped me gather eggs from the Field of Giants, and many of them have tales of how deadly the creatures are. I've heard enough to consider them insects a much larger threat than my masters first thought.\nI need a courier to travel to Orgrimmar to meet Belgrom Rockmaul. It be no simple matter, and someone who would take the task seriously should go.\nBelgrom usually be found outside the warriors' guild house.","rew":"Experience: 1,300\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I envy you, ‹class›. You have the look of someone who's been outside the walls of Orgrimmar for a while.\nI myself would travel in the name of the Warchief if Thrall didn't have need of my skills here in the city. But he leads us well, and I trust his judgement - I remain here for as long as he needs me.","done":"Ah, a note from Korran. He has been a loyal servant for some time now. I was wondering how his duties were going in the Crossroads.\nThe Barrens Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.1,"y":29.6,"n":"Korran","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":75.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Belgrom Rockmaul","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1065":{"id":1065,"t":"Journey to Tarren Mill","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Zamah's Note to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.\nZamah's Note\nProvided: Zamah's Note","desc":"To rid Stonetalon of the Venture Company, we must take extreme measures. Extreme, but without bloodshed.\nA colleague of mine may have just the tool we need. His name is Lydon; he dwells in the town of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills, in the distant land of Lordaeron.\nTo reach Hillsbrad, travel by zeppelin to our capital, the Undercity. Then go north to Tirisfal Glades, southwest to Silverpine, and south to Hillsbrad.\nSeek Lydon and bring him this note. It details our needs to him.","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Ah, are you here with my new test subjects?","done":"A note from Zamah? Her needs must be great to send word from so far. Let us see what she says...\nAh, splendid! I know exactly what to do!\nThunder Bluff Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":22.8,"y":20.9,"n":"Apothecary Zamah","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"7625":{"id":7625,"t":"Xorothian Stardust","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Purchase Xorothian Stardust from Ur'dan. Bring it to Gorzeeki Wildeyes in the Burning Steppes.\nXorothian Stardust sold by Ur'dan","desc":"So you come to me seeking Xorothian stardust? You wish to open a portal to Xoroth, the domain of Hel'nurath my rival? Perhaps you plan to steal from him one of his precious dreadsteeds?\nVery well. My servant Ur'dan has a supply of Xorothian stardust. You may obtain it from him... if you can pay the price.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Have you been to Jaedenar, ‹name›? Did you get the stardust from Lord Banehollow?","done":"There it is! I can hardly believe you got it! You must have struck a big deal with that Dreadlord or else paid a large sum, or both!\nMor'zul will have his ink very soon and then he can finally make the glyph parchment, so you can open a portal to Xoroth and pull through it one of the famed dreadsteeds!\nFelwood Burning Steppes","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":35.9,"y":44.4,"n":"Lord Banehollow","s":1},{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Gorzeeki Wildeyes","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"3065":{"id":3065,"t":"Simple Tablet","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Simple Tablet and speak to Frang in the Valley of Trials.\nSimple Tablet\nProvided: Simple Tablet","desc":"Ah, while you were gone a parchment came for you, ‹name›.\nRead it when you have time. If I'm not mistaken, it came from the warrior trainer Frang. He would have words with you when you're ready. You'll find him outside the Den, taking cover in the shade.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Another troll to bolster the ranks. Good enough for me.\nYou'll probably have a hard time hefting a good weapon like an axe, but a spear's just as good as anything else.\nWelcome to the Valley of Trials.","done":"You'll find this place fitting as you continue to train in the warrior ways. If you have any questions, feel free to ask anyone around, and when you feel you're ready, come back to me for training. I've mastered as much as any warrior here in the Valley and can pass that knowledge on to you... for a price.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":42.9,"y":69.4,"n":"Frang","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1705":{"id":1705,"t":"Burning Blood","lv":28,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 vials of Burning Blood and 1 Burning Rock to Grimand Elmore in Stormwind.\n20 Burning Blood Nightbane Tainted One 80 % , Nightbane Worgen 80 % , Nightbane Shadow Weaver 80 % , Nightbane Vile Fang 80 % and 1 more\nBurning Rock Gutspill 80 %","desc":"I hate to admit that Furen might have really found something. But to be sure I'll need to try his techniques on a new piece of armor. If you help me with the materials, ‹name›, then you can have the armor.\nTo make this armor, I need samples of burning blood and a burning rock.\nThe only place I know to get them is Duskwood. The Nightbane worgen based in the Roland's Doom mine have burning blood, and their leader Gutspill will have the rock.\nMay fortune grant you speed, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 2,300","back":"‹name›, do you have the burning blood and rock? I'll need them to complete the armor.","done":"Nice work! Now if you'll excuse me, I have some work to do myself...\nStormwind City Duskwood","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":59.7,"y":33.8,"n":"Grimand Elmore","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8425":{"id":8425,"t":"Voodoo Feathers","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Voodoo Feathers from the trolls in the Sunken Temple to the Fallen Hero of the Horde.\n2 Amber Voodoo Feather Gasher , Zul'Lor\n2 Blue Voodoo Feather Hukku , Mijan\n2 Green Voodoo Feather Zolo , Loro","desc":"Your honor has brought some peace to me. It is only right that I offer you something in return.\nMy weapons and armor were splendid in life, and yet they are of no use to me now. They would be better served in your possession.\nTravel to the sunken temple and destroy the troll guardians Gasher, Mijan, Zolo, Hukku, Zul'lor, and Loro. They carry magic feathers that can reform my physical body long enough to grant you a reward.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFury Visor Diamond Flask Razorsteel Shoulders\nExperience: 6,350","back":"Are you back so soon? Time is not the same to me any more, perhaps it has indeed been a long journey for you...","done":"At last I can feel the cold touch of steel again, even if only for a moment.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"4985":{"id":4985,"t":"The Wildlife Suffers Too","lv":56,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Destroy 8 Diseased Grizzlies, and then return to Mulgris Deepriver at the Writhing Haunt, Western Plaguelands.\nDiseased Grizzly slain : 0/ 8","desc":"To the east of where we are, near where the Eastern Plaguelands begin, once proud and majestic grizzlies roamed the countryside. The plague released by the Scourge has sundered these beasts too. They wander the countryside, agonized by the stiffening of their muscles and the rotting of their fur and flesh.\nI ask of you to end their misery as well. The only cure for their suffering is a swift death, one that must be ministered by your hand.","rew":"Experience: 4,350\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"I hear your footsteps, ‹name›. My vision has faded from me, but I still am able to sense things around me. Have you ended the misery of the disease-ridden grizzlies?","done":"\"I know that the grizzles have been put down, their torment at an end. I... I have one more thing for you. I wrote it down on... on this branch, sensing that my time in this realm had come to an end.\nIndeed... I am at that end. Thank you again friend... the creatures of this accursed land may rest... and now shall I.\"\nWith that, a heavy sigh is uttered by the druid, followed by what sounds like a death rattle. His body lies motionless on the cottage floor.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":53.7,"y":64.7,"n":"Mulgris Deepriver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5225":{"id":5225,"t":"Target: Gahrron's Withering","lv":58,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to Gahrron's Withering in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron. You must have the Empty Gahrron's Withering Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\nGahrron's Withering Cauldron Key Cauldron Lord Soulwrath\nEmpty Gahrron's Withering Bottle\nProvided: Empty Gahrron's Withering Bottle","desc":"The last cauldron that remains is located on a farm now called Gahrron's Withering. It is guarded by some of the Scourge's tougher minions - specifically, wraiths and ghosts. They are not to be trifled with, ‹name›.\nGahrron's Withering is due northeast of our position here, close to where the Eastern Plaguelands begin; again, eliminate the cauldron lord present there for its key. Here is your empty sample bottle; bring it to me filled. May the Light protect you in this dangerous mission, ‹class›.","rew":"Experience: 6,200\n+100 reputation with Stormwind\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened. In order to open it, you will need to find the key.","done":"Cauldron Lord Soulwrath's key disintegrates as it touches the lock on the access panel at the base of the cauldron's platform. A slight clanking noise is heard within, and the access panel swings open to reveal more viscous toxins within the cauldron's framework.\nThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for High Priestess MacDonnell back at Chillwind Point.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43,"y":84.5,"n":"High Priestess MacDonnell","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":62.5,"y":58.5,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"6025":{"id":6025,"t":"Unfinished Business","lv":58,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Enter Hearthglen and find a high vantage point from which you can see the town and gauge the Scarlet Crusade's forces, then return to Kirsta Deepshadow in Western Plaguelands.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"What? Really? You want to know more? But you've already done so much for me, ‹name›. I couldn't possibly ask you to enter Hearthglen itself on my behalf.\nAre you sure, ‹name›? Hearthglen is much more dangerous than the Pass--I cannot provide you any protection or even information about what you might face.\nWell, if you really are willing to help, then enter the town and find a high place to gain a good view of the town. From there you can gauge their numbers and report them back to me. But be careful....","rew":"Money: 1 75 1 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,200","back":"It's a dangerous task, ‹name›. I envy your courage.","done":"You've done it, ‹name›! Thank you!\nI'll return to Elling... I mean Stormwind as soon as I can. Here, take this coin, it's the least I can do for you. You're a credit to your people, ‹name›. Thank you and good luck.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":51.9,"y":28.1,"n":"Kirsta Deepshadow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"105":{"id":105,"t":"Alas, Andorhal","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Araj's Phylactery Shard to High Executor Derrington at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\nAraj's Phylactery Shard Araj's Phylactery","desc":"Alas, the time to attack Andorhal and drive out the lich that controls it is upon us!\nInside the ruins of the city is where the lich - Araj the Summoner - holds dominion. He is guarded by numerous Scourge surrounding the remains of city's center, and his personal retinue of guardians attached to him directly is formidable. You will need numerous allies to even stand a chance of facing him successfully.\nDestroy Araj, ‹name›, and bring me a shard from his phylactery as proof!","rew":"You will receive:\nMark of Resolution\nExperience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Horde\n+150 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Your task has been given to you, ‹name›. Do you have a shard from the lich's phylactery as proof of the task being accomplished?","done":"You've done it! Araj... the lich is finally defeated!\nYou've done a tremendous service to the Horde on this day, ‹name›. Your bravery and perseverance are a testament to what it means to be a true hero. Please - accept this as a token for all to see and know that you have delivered the Horde a victory for the ages!\nTirisfal Glades Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.1,"y":68.9,"n":"High Executor Derrington","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5465":{"id":5465,"t":"Soulbound Keepsake","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 4,950 experience instead of 5,300, 0.93 times as much.","obj":"Return to Magistrate Marduke in Caer Darrow. Show him the Soulbound Keepsake.\nSoulbound Keepsake\nProvided: Soulbound Keepsake","desc":"Return to Marduke with the keepsake, ‹name›. He will instruct you in its use.","rew":"Experience: 4,950","back":"Have you done the impossible?","done":"I was certain that you would be joining me as another hapless spirit.\nEastern Plaguelands Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.9,"y":48.3,"n":"Leonid Barthalomew the Revered","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":70.6,"y":74.1,"n":"Magistrate Marduke","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"92745":{"id":92745,"t":"The state of the mines","lv":14,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 4 Kobold Diggers in the Jangolode Mine and 6 Riverpaw Miners in the Gold Coast Quarry.\nKobold Digger slain : 0/ 4\nRiverpaw Miner slain : 0/ 6","desc":"The well samples you collected contain toxic metals! If we do not put an end to this corruption quickly, it will be decades before crops can grow in this soil again.\nThe Defias have seized the mines of Westfall and use creatures as labor to strip their resources. Disrupt them by slaying their miners in the Jangolode Mine to the north, and the Gold Coast Quarry to the west.","rew":"Money: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 490\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Well done, Xeph. But I fear the source of the poison may lie somewhere else...","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":52.4,"y":53,"n":"Alba Fairmoon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"93065":{"id":93065,"t":"Prepare for battle","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Valennia Stormfist in the Gustberry Lowlands.\nFind Valennia on the Road","desc":"The Peacekeepers are mobilizing and we are all gearing up to head out. Make whatever preparations you need to make and meet us at the eastern road leading north out of town. We'll have one final check-in with everyone before we move out.","done":"We are as ready as we'll ever be.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":76.6,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":61.2,"y":71,"n":"Valennia Stormfist","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8185":{"id":8185,"t":"Syncretist's Sigil","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring me thise things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!\nPrimal Hakkari Idol\nPunctured Voodoo Doll\nPrimal Hakkari Idol Jin'do the Hexxer in Zul'Gurub , Bloodlord Mandokir in Zul'Gurub\nPunctured Voodoo Doll Zulian Stalker 0.3 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadow Hunter 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadowcaster 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Zealot Lor'Khan 0 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more","desc":"Zanza can create the ancient troll enchantments with the right components. The first is a primal Hakkari idol that must be taken from the most powerful of the Hakkari lieutenants: Jin'do and the Bloodlord.\nThe second is a punctured voodoo doll. These can be found in the piles of refuse that litter this foul place. Look inside the jinxed hoodoo.\nBring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","rew":"You will receive:\nSyncretist's Sigil\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Bring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","done":"Use it well, ‹class›. Show the Hakkari no mercy!\nStart Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub End Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub Level 60 , requires level 58 Difficulty 58 Side Alliance Type Raid Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8185","cats":["zulgurub"]}});